# The pc platform's gem path test (#1093, docs/platforms.md), played with
# --level 11 --room gem-path (Ace of Space's gem path, the one HOVER room):
# boot.keys's Start and A through the logos and menus to the level select,
# which picks the level (its last Start pauses it, A at 524 resumes), then
# the hover ride, steered with the D-pad (left slows the ride and puts the
# camera lead 50 px ahead, right 10 px, neither 30 px) past a ? crate and
# a nitro wall, through the nitro field until a nitro kills Crash (~1024),
# then on foot in the level's first room, where a TNT crate kills him
# (~1240). The ride crashed the host on its first frame until SetLeadSpeed's
# NULL_WRITE and the camera lead's NULL_READs (its sprite has no bank).
# tools/boottest.py `screens` (the same --level and --room) played it on
# mGBA for tests/gem_path_mgba_screens.json.
# Written by a search over the host's runs (the steering that kept Crash
# alive longest).
# A line `FRAME KEYS` holds KEYS from FRAME on (platform/pc/src/input.c).
